invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_blocks.c
catches: rsa_blocks_equiv_test
reason: block_mul_add drops the carry out of its low chain, the carry from
  the four products' low halves into the word above the block, so the
  word it returns is one short whenever that chain carries, which random
  words do about half the time. bin/rsa_blocks_equiv_test runs the blocks
  under any compiler and compares their words with rsa_mont64.c's loops.

--- old
    return (uint64_t)(p3 >> 64) + low_carry + (uint64_t)(sum >> 64);
--- new
    return (uint64_t)(p3 >> 64) + (low_carry & 0) + (uint64_t)(sum >> 64);
